Description: Stop the session bus at the end of the session also while a start job of a service which needs it is queued.
 gnome-session-restart-dbus.service stops dbus.service at the end of the session, so that the next login starts a new
 session bus. gnome-session-ctl asks systemd for the stop with the job mode "fail", which systemd refuses when the stop
 conflicts with a queued job, as when a D-Bus activation during the shutdown queued the start of a service which needs
 dbus.service. Desktop Icons NG starts its process again while GNOME Shell shuts down, which starts
 xdg-desktop-portal, whose start job stays queued because its GNOME backend cannot start once the graphical session
 has ended. The session bus then stays, and the next login uses it. The stop now replaces such jobs.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-23

--- a/tools/gnome-session-ctl.c
+++ b/tools/gnome-session-ctl.c
@@ -123,6 +123,10 @@
         if (connection == NULL)
                 return;
 
+        /* A D-Bus activation during the shutdown of the session can queue the
+         * start of a service which needs dbus.service, such as a portal whose
+         * backend cannot start anymore. The stop replaces such a job, as it
+         * would otherwise fail and leave the bus to the next login. */
         reply = g_dbus_connection_call_sync (connection,
                                              SYSTEMD_DBUS,
                                              SYSTEMD_PATH_DBUS,
@@ -130,7 +134,7 @@
                                              "StopUnit",
                                              g_variant_new ("(ss)",
                                                             "dbus.service",
-                                                            "fail"),
+                                                            "replace"),
                                              NULL,
                                              G_DBUS_CALL_FLAGS_NO_AUTO_START,
                                              -1, NULL, &error);
